{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-condition--1","instance--0c9a6a38-c003-504e-8826-6c524a58ab0c","vulnerability--cve-2025-49706","vulnerability--cve-2025-49704","instance--413c9750-5c28-52c5-ba5f-59a5ed51ffde","instance--ea4ffbfc-2cfe-55a0-96c3-cde4c6a8d5c6","process--powershell-exe","software--iis","instance--07f9550c-3e26-5d19-a2eb-81ae3dc25d92","instance--880928dc-28be-531d-a412-15144a85eceb","software--sharpyshell","instance--9fc90ed3-24ab-5aaa-a687-bab7b3264223","instance--2829b832-e256-5647-9a16-e5a5eb8728b8","software--tool-1","instance--ecd2c858-4644-5aed-9a01-c9e50dbb7a7b","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--98ad2859-e025-535b-9136-fcd2527f8618","instance--5420b01a-427f-54a1-be1f-788e3ad6229d","instance--753cbb9d-54dc-539c-a02e-3584e6756a1a","instance--5d2fc85e-cc07-5a4b-aa12-9082a6b20f38","instance--4e2c8b00-4a1a-5324-910a-99302a1cf15c","instance--f74373cc-0da6-5045-a713-1aa0685f8f81","instance--b7057231-445a-5a60-bcfe-d44a954e31a8","instance--48bd56df-cfc6-56a5-8f83-eb24ceb1b848","instance--f5afbdb1-26e6-5900-a8f0-3fc7a849ec52","instance--12de56b4-8874-5dca-8769-3ee533bea109","instance--8e28a1ae-0647-5431-9ef3-35ba6db4d569","instance--6c6b07cc-68a7-5965-8f16-ab45927d5ebb","instance--7ee7fa41-9325-50f1-9dda-44f541a02478","instance--ceda8a7d-3023-517a-87b5-ede76527b9ba","instance--64793d13-6d53-5659-8e68-fe1ed4074ff3","instance--e3e14edc-f0e3-5c15-92fe-e61d79ceaa06"],"properties":[["name","SharePoint Under Siege: ToolShell Exploit (CVE-2025-49706 & CVE-2025-49704)"],["description","Eye Security research describing in-the-wild exploitation of the ToolShell chain against on-premise SharePoint servers."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Eye Security"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","research.eye.security"],["url","https://research.eye.security/sharepoint-under-siege/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Exploit ToolShell for unauthenticated RCE"],["description","After some digging, we learned that three days earlier, the offensive security team from they could reproduce an unauthenticated RCE exploit chain in SharePoint, a combination of two bugs presented at Pwn2Own Berlin earlier this year in May: CVE-2025-49706 & CVE-2025-49704. They dubbed the chain .\n\nAt the time, it was considered a proof-of-concept. No public code was released, and details were scarce. But the timing matched. And so did the behavior: vulnerability in , file writes, no login, and complete control of the web application process."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1190"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Write malicious ASPX web shell"],["description","Early in the evening, our 24/7 detection team received an alert from one of our deployment at a specific customer. The alert flagged a suspicious process chain on a legacy SharePoint on-prem server, tied to a recently uploaded malicious file.\n\nAt first glance, it looked familiar. A classic web shell, obfuscated code in a custom path, designed to allow remote command execution via HTTP."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Spawn PowerShell from IIS worker"],["description","Powershell.exe process spawned by as grandparent (IIS worker) and as parent on the affected Windows Server (telemetry collected by our EDR):\n\nDecoding reveals the payload, unpacking a base64 layer and dropping its contents to :"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Drop SharpyShell payload"],["description","Decoding reveals the payload, unpacking a base64 layer and dropping its contents to :\n\nContents of , most probably created with (92bb4ddb98eeaf11fc15bb32e71d0a63256a0ed826a03ba293ce3a8bf057a514)"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Dump SharePoint cryptographic secrets"],["description","Instead, what we discovered was more subtle, and arguably more dangerous: a stealthy file whose sole purpose was to extract and leak cryptographic secrets from the SharePoint server using a simple GET request.\n\nThis wasn\u2019t your typical webshell. There were no interactive commands, reverse shells, or command-and-control logic. Instead, the page invoked internal .NET methods to read the SharePoint server\u2019s configuration, including the . These keys are essential for generating valid payloads, and gaining access to them effectively turns any authenticated SharePoint request into a ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1552"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Craft signed SharePoint payloads with leaked keys"],["description","Now, using the ToolShell chain (CVE-2025-49706 + CVE-2025-49704), the attackers we observed were able to extract the via the malicious ASPX. Once this cryptographic material is leaked, the attacker can craft fully valid, signed payloads using a tool called as shown in the example below. Using the attacker can its own valid SharePoint tokens for RCE:\n\nThese payloads can embed any malicious commands. It allows for full persistence and zero authentication, even after patching."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1606.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Once this cryptographic material is leaked, the attacker can craft fully valid, signed payloads using a tool called as shown in the example below."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--9e9c2fce-5656-5d61-82eb-380610a2c217","120":"instance--1a1d5041-24a7-5693-b28b-dce237ffd027","150":"instance--a74de142-93a9-5252-8468-73ddce73f132","180":"instance--946861ac-01db-5e47-9a14-ea790375b8fe","210":"instance--f1d2e37d-f3fb-5e78-b3dc-0a5ad1822d8e","240":"instance--abb0ffd0-553e-5984-81d5-ad0ab6d5f196","270":"instance--f1bfee0d-6f15-5d24-94e6-2a101c38735d","30":"instance--f68c3cfb-8be1-57ee-b21a-2029f062e32b","300":"instance--a8217483-44b2-5168-90a0-6b96bce30cf2","330":"instance--919ba284-0fc0-53fb-a10b-aa9188dbf848","60":"instance--606cb111-5932-543e-899f-33497ce26de9","90":"instance--8b422f0a-278f-5cd5-b472-c3b03021c649"},"id":"software","instance":"instance--0c9a6a38-c003-504e-8826-6c524a58ab0c","properties":[["vendor","Microsoft"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"this exploit is being used to compromise on-premise SharePoint Servers across the world.","source":"https://research.eye.security/sharepoint-under-siege/","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","SharePoint Server"],["name","SharePoint Server"],["diagram_instance","instance--0c9a6a38-c003-504e-8826-6c524a58ab0c"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--e0451e96-bd73-5e6d-92b5-058f48fd5d50","120":"instance--21e02d6e-463c-528c-93f5-68c41f6f8daa","150":"instance--d3871290-22f5-5800-a811-3d1c35635742","180":"instance--29486fce-c62a-5542-b7a5-44b2305b9ade","210":"instance--5c592517-1cf3-5d8e-af7b-c3e68ea24de2","240":"instance--750bcd1f-858c-5335-b704-4514c99680f9","270":"instance--381e79bd-880e-53ff-893a-e968fb26b80a","30":"instance--762b3084-1fd0-58d9-b402-3efa1a18e2e7","300":"instance--42d20e22-fe8a-5f6c-98aa-8d7f7c899e47","330":"instance--ef5c057a-ef55-53a1-b4a3-e533df66c9c1","60":"instance--494c3e8d-1d49-5e52-80d5-5b66c8a87511","90":"instance--d7491c24-e0bd-5488-8030-3c2a61498654"},"id":"vulnerability","instance":"vulnerability--cve-2025-49706","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"The vulnerabilities exploited during the July 17\u201319 seem not to be CVE-2025-53770/53771, but rather the original ToolShell chain: CVE-2025-49706 (auth bypass) and CVE-2025-49704 (deserialization RCE).","source":"https://research.eye.security/sharepoint-under-siege/","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","CVE-2025-49706"],["name","CVE-2025-49706"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--d4e5b33b-0963-58b3-a1af-ed88e24de0e2","120":"instance--9ccb7d25-3bad-593a-9687-65dacd642bff","150":"instance--fca9184f-f771-5a43-9eb0-9c3e52fc4b55","180":"instance--90e708cf-d159-5e4b-9f9e-78f7158a6bca","210":"instance--8042ac62-5e24-55da-a384-117521e18b5f","240":"instance--9680962b-777f-56eb-8d23-8f535aded7c3","270":"instance--bb829533-a387-5750-a9af-bc5b46ceb0f6","30":"instance--17edc437-92ec-5acd-88da-436cca78b38d","300":"instance--cdc3e3c0-9bfc-5af8-83d9-53682d83ee33","330":"instance--2413bdaa-e56c-5684-9323-636ccc7c69b1","60":"instance--a9eb1ee2-7971-5ee2-8531-1d5b46b3b280","90":"instance--e56cc01f-3432-5e5b-844f-89c9e4363106"},"id":"vulnerability","instance":"vulnerability--cve-2025-49704","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"The vulnerabilities exploited during the July 17\u201319 seem not to be CVE-2025-53770/53771, but rather the original ToolShell chain: CVE-2025-49706 (auth bypass) and CVE-2025-49704 (deserialization RCE).","source":"https://research.eye